<span class="line" data-line="40"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">  token_rotation_enabled</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">:</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-constant)"> false</span></span></code></pre><button class="invisible absolute right-4 border border-gray-new-80 bg-white p-1.5 text-gray-new-40 opacity-0 transition-[background-color,opacity,visibility] duration-200 group-hover/code-block:visible group-hover/code-block:opacity-100 hover:bg-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:bg-black-pure dark:text-gray-new-60 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8 lg:visible lg:opacity-100 top-4" type="button" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="h-3.5 w-3.5 text-current"><rect width="8.995" height="9.002" x="5.939" y="5.935" stroke="currentColor" rx="1"></rect><path fill="currentColor" fill-rule="evenodd" d="M2.434.935a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5 1.5v7.001a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.5 1.5h1.499a.5.5 0 0 0 0-1h-1.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V2.435a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5h6.995a.5.5 0 0 1 .5.5v1.5a.5.5 0 1 0 1 0v-1.5a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-1.5-1.5z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path></svg></button></figure>
<p>This manifest defines how your bot can communicate in Slack. Some key configurations to note:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>oauth_config.scopes</code> sets the permissions your bot needs to read mentions and post replies.</li>
<li><code>event_subscriptions.bot_events</code> tells Slack which events should trigger webhook calls.</li>
<li><code>request_url</code> points Slack to your local webhook endpoint exposed through ngrok.</li>
<li><code>interactivity.request_url</code> enables interactive payloads (buttons, actions, and some rich responses).</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>Replace <code>https://&lt;your-ngrok-id&gt;.ngrok.app</code> with your actual ngrok forwarding URL from <a class="" href="#start-ngrok">previous step</a>.</p>
</blockquote>
</li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong> and then <strong>Create</strong> to create your Slack App with the specified configuration.</p>
<p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Slack App Manifest" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" src="/docs/guides/slack_app_manifest.png?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Navigate to <strong>OAuth &amp; Permissions</strong> in the left sidebar, click <strong>Install to Workspace</strong> under <strong>OAuth Tokens</strong>, and copy the <strong>Bot User OAuth Token</strong> (it will start with <code>xoxb-</code>).
<span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Bot User OAuth Token" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" src="/docs/guides/slack_bot_token.png?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Navigate to <strong>Basic Information</strong> &gt; <strong>App Credentials</strong> and copy your <strong>Signing Secret</strong>.</p>
</li>
